  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened social protection system in Sierra Leone</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In Sierra Leone, there are fragmented implementation of social protection programmes and schemes. In terms of social protection programmes, there are some non-contributory social assistance programmes for the most vulnerable segment of the society while there are schemes for workers in the formal sector, however, there no schemes or coverage for people and workers in the informal sector. The ILO is supporting the government to review it social protection programmes to expand coverage especially for people in the informal sector.

The strategy focuses on developing capacity for social protection coverage for the government including NASSIT, the workers&#x2019; and employers&#x2019; organisations, developing and implementing appropriate and flexible social protection schemes.</narrative>
  </description>
